{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>A vicious beast has devoured him.</b> This hints at encompassing the tribes, who were likened to beasts — lion, hind, and serpent — and Scripture encompasses them all and says (Ezekiel 19:2) ״מָה אִמְּךָ לְבִיאָה בֵּין אֲרָיוֹת״. Another interpretation: 'A vicious beast' — this is the evil report that he brought, how his brothers ate a limb from a living animal; this evil report (דִּבָּה רָעָה) is hinted at in 'a beast (חַיָּה) has devoured him,' for they sought to show that the matter was not so, but rather ״וַיִּשְׁחֲטוּ שְׂעִיר עִזִּים״. And all this was from the spirit of holy inspiration that sparkled in him, for even according to Rashi's interpretation, who explained 'a vicious beast' as referring to the wife of Potiphar, the spirit of HaShem spoke through him. But behold, the matter of Potiphar's wife had not yet occurred — so how could he say 'devoured him' in the past tense? And moreover, what is the relevance of that matter here? Rather, the correct reading is as we have written."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:32:21.843932605Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}